  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Rakesh Kumar vs State Of U.P. And Another on 10 January, 2020 Author: Rajiv Gupta Bench: Rajiv Gupta High Court Of Judicature At Allahabad ?Court No. - 75 Case :- Application U/S 482 No. - 1334 of 2020 Applicant :- Rakesh Kumar",
    "facts": "As per the allegation made in the complaint, it is alleged that the sample collected from the shop of the applicant was found to be harmful for human consumption, as such proceeding has been initiated against the applicant and he was summoned under Sections 3(1) (2Z) (iv) and 6(2) (1), 59 (1) of Food Safety and Standards Act 2006 vide order dated 30.4.2014. Pursuant to the said order dated 30.4.2014, the applicant appeared before the Court and has been granted bail.",
    "arguments": "Learned counsel for the applicant has submitted that proceedings initiated against the applicant is without any basis and only because some harmful substance has been found in the sample, proceedings under the Food Safety and Standards Act cannot be drawn against him. Per contra, learned AGA has submitted that on the basis of sample report submitted by the designated officer, the proceedings has rightly been initiated against the applicant and there is no illegality in the said order. Moreover, the present application has been filed with the delay of more than six years and there is no explanation for the laches in filing the present application and as such, no interference is required.",
    "petitioner_arguments": "Learned counsel for the applicant has submitted that proceedings initiated against the applicant is without any basis and only because some harmful substance has been found in the sample, proceedings under the Food Safety and Standards Act cannot be drawn against him. Per contra, learned AGA has submitted that on the basis of sample report submitted by the designated officer, the proceedings has rightly been initiated against the applicant and there is no illegality in the said order. Moreover, the present application has been filed with the delay of more than six years and there is no explanation for the laches in filing the present application and as such, no interference is required.",
    "respondent_arguments": "",
    "other_lawyer_arguments": ""
  },
